{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Types Of Routing :-\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\tab 1. Attribute Routing :- [Route] [HttpGet]\par
\tab 2. Conventional Routing :- Central route configuration\par
\tab 3. Http Method Routing\par
\tab 4. Parametrized Routing :- [HttpGet("\{id\}")]\par
\b\par
\b0 Lecture :- ( HTTP Status Codes in ASP.NET Core Web API )\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Standard response codes returned by server to indicate request result\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}basically it tells client whether request succeeded or failed\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}200 OK :- request successfull\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}201 Created :- resource successfully created\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}204 No Content :- request successful but nor response body\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}400 Bad Request :- client sent invalid request\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}401 Unauthorized :- authentication requierd\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}403 Forbidden :=- authenticated but access deined\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}404 Not Found :- resource not found\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}500 Internal Server Error :- server side error occured\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b Lecture :- ( Model Binding in ASP.NET Core Web API )\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b0 Its a process of automatically mapping http request data to action method parameter or mdoel objects\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b Lecture :- ( Lazy Loading in Entity Framework Core )\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 There are three types of loading :-\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\tab 1. Lazy Loading :- Load related data only when we accessed only specific class\par
\tab 2. Eager Loading :- Load immediately\par
\tab 3. Explicit Loading :- Load Manually when needed\par
Lazy Loading :-\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Related data is loaded automatically only when accessed for the first time\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Example :- ( N + 1 ) query problem\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 var customer = context.Customers.FirstOrDefault();\par
Here above only data of customers get only load , but not of orders but below when we accessed data of orders then only it loads and here ef core automatically firesd another sql query\par
var orders = customer.Orders;\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Dynamic proxy classess ( Pending )\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Eager Loading :-\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Loads related data immediately and for this we use Include()\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 var customers = context.Customers\par
                       .Include(c => c.Orders)\par
                       .ToList();\par
\par
\b Lecture :- ( Explicit Loading in Entity Framework Core )\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b0 Explicit loading means related data is loaded manually and explicitly by developer when needed\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Example :- You manually call waiter and order only when needed.'\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Its a kind of customization version\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 context.Entry(customer)\par
       .Collection(c => c.Orders)\par
       .Load()\par

